# This directory is intentionally empty for now.
#
# It must exist: `Package.swift` declares a `JanelaClientTests` target, and SwiftPM
# warns about a target whose sources directory is missing.
#
# What belongs here (docs/testing.md):
#
#   - `AttentionPolicy`, exhaustively. It is pure, synchronous logic and every rule
#     in docs/decisions/0011-notifications.md is one test: no delivery for the
#     focused terminal in an active app, no delivery for a bare bell, delivery for
#     an explicit OSC 9, no delivery for a fast command that failed, one delivery
#     for the same signal seen twice.
#   - Mirror updates: a full snapshot replaces state, a partial update merges by id,
#     and `selection` survives both because it is client-only state that never
#     travels.
#   - `isRunning` is derived from what the daemon reported, never inferred from what
#     this client did.
#   - Reconnect: backoff, re-subscribe, and a full snapshot replacing a stale mirror.
#     Test with the transport failing mid-frame, which is what a daemon restart
#     looks like from here.
#   - `.refused` is terminal until the user acts. A client that automatically
#     restarts the daemon on a version mismatch would kill live terminals, which is
#     the one thing we promised never to do.
#
# Use an in-memory `MessageTransport` here so these stay deterministic. The daemon
# side uses a real socket, so the pairing is covered somewhere — faking both sides
# would test nothing.
